<https://research.tib.eu/ldm/8b833e4d-ef22-4acd-a6d3-d13e7cd9d883> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "contain the negative triples constructed for positive ones in the validation sets, with a positive-to-negative ratio of 1:10. They are used only in triple classification.\nThe fb122_triples.neg.valid files contains one triple per line, stored in a tab (\\'\\t\\') separated format. The first element is the head entity, the second the relation, and the third the tail entity.".
